 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging on a Roomba E5 is most commonly caused by dirty contacts between the robot and the base station. Dust or debris can prevent a good connection, causing it to charge sometimes but not others. Please try this simple check first: unplug the base station, then wipe the gold-coloured metal charging plates on the bottom of your Roomba and the corresponding contacts on the base with a dry cloth. Ensure they are clean and dry before plugging it back in. Also, check if the power brick (the black box on the cable) gets very hot or if the light on the base station behaves erratically (flashing instead of staying solid). Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok did that. contacts were dull with a greasy film and lots of hair on the robot ones. after wiping it's charged 4 nights in a row now, no error. power brick isn't hot and the base light comes on when it docks"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. It sounds like the greasy film and hair were preventing a solid electrical connection between the robot and the base station. To help stop this happening again, try giving those contacts a quick wipe with a dry cloth every few weeks or whenever you notice it taking longer to start charging. If it starts acting up again after that, let me know."
  }
 ],
